---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Structure with intention" description="Kōshi is a lightweight, dependency-free CSS grid system for thoughtful responsive layouts. Explore the documentation and interactive Composition Lab.">
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero-section">
      <span class="eyebrow">A modern CSS grid system — 格子</span>
      <h1 class="display">Structure<br /><em>with intention.</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">A lightweight, flexible CSS grid system for crafting thoughtful, responsive layouts. No framework required. Just CSS, proportion, and room to experiment.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="action action-primary" href="/docs/">Get started ↗</a>
        <a class="action action-outline" href="/downloads/koshi.css" download="koshi.css">Download CSS ↓</a>
        <a class="action action-outline" href="/lab/">Explore the Lab ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="system-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="eyebrow">01 / THE SYSTEM</span><span class="eyebrow">12 COLUMNS · ONE FOUNDATION</span></div>
      <h2 id="system-title" class="section-title">An underlying rhythm.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Start with twelve tracks. Divide the space into deliberate proportions, or let an intrinsic grid respond to the available room.</p>
      <div class="grid-demonstration">
        <div class="demo-meta"><span>GRID / 12 COLUMNS</span><span>8 + 4 = 12</span></div>
        <div class="demo-grid" aria-label="An eight-column area beside a four-column area"><div class="feature"><span>08 / 12</span></div><div class="aside"><span>04 / 12</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="explore-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="eyebrow">02 / EXPLORE</span><span class="eyebrow">FROM FOUNDATION TO FORM</span></div>
      <h2 id="explore-title" class="section-title">Make space for ideas.</h2>
      <div class="feature-links">
        <a class="feature-link" href="/docs/"><span class="number">01 / LEARN</span><div><h3>Documentation ↗</h3><p>Understand columns, spans, gutters, offsets, and responsive compositions.</p></div></a>
        <a class="feature-link" href="/lab/"><span class="number">02 / EXPLORE</span><div><h3>Composition Lab ↗</h3><p>Browse editorial layout studies and copy structures into your own work.</p></div></a>
        <a class="feature-link" href="/downloads/koshi.css" download="koshi.css"><span class="number">03 / BUILD</span><div><h3>Download Kōshi ↓</h3><p>Take the standalone CSS file. No JavaScript, Vue, or Astro required.</p></div></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="padding-bottom: 115px" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <div class="section-label"><span class="eyebrow">03 / GET STARTED</span><span class="eyebrow">PLAIN HTML + CSS</span></div>
      <h2 id="start-title" class="section-title">Start with the grid.</h2>
      <pre class="code-sample"><code>{`<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/koshi.css" />

<div class="kos-grid">
  <main kos-col-span="8">Your content</main>
  <aside kos-col-span="4">A supporting space</aside>
</div>`}</code></pre>
      <div class="actions"><a class="action action-outline" href="/docs/">Read the documentation ↗</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
